# Line endings are LF, in the repository AND in the working tree, on every
# platform. `text=auto` alone only fixed the repository side and left checkout
# to core.autocrlf, which is true on the Windows dev machine: git kept warning
# that it would rewrite LF files as CRLF, and the working tree drifted into a
# mix of CRLF, LF and both-at-once files. `eol=lf` settles it, and it is the
# right default here anyway since everything runs on Linux inside Docker.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text files (LF everywhere, per the rule above)
*.py    text
*.sql   text
*.md    text
*.sh    text
*.txt   text
*.json  text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.cfg   text
*.ini   text
*.env   text
Dockerfile text

# Binary files (never normalized)
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.pdf   binary
